cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this research code and data package when using the associated implementation or saved evidence."
type: dataset
title: 'Research Code and Data for "Identifiable Directed Contributions in Multi-RIS Scattering: Receiver-Only Estimation and Calibrated Reliability"'
authors:
  - family-names: Liu
    given-names: Ziming
    affiliation: "BELL Honors College, Nanjing University of Posts and Telecommunications"
    email: "zimmyliuu@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zimmyliuu/multi-ris-directed-contributions"
url: "https://zenodo.org/records/23357653"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23357653"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-10-14
abstract: >-
  Curated research implementation, frozen simulation results, calibration
  records, and figure-reproduction inputs accompanying the manuscript by
  Ziming Liu. Includes 900 fresh paired confirmation geometries and SHA256
  integrity verification. The scientific scope is identifiable coexisting
  directed RIS contributions under the stated quasistatic scalar model,
  receiver-only estimation, and distribution-specific calibrated reliability.
  The package does not establish general unknown-topology recovery or hardware
  validation.
keywords:
  - reconfigurable intelligent surfaces
  - channel estimation
  - identifiability
  - inverse scattering
  - risk calibration
  - selective inference
